---
// Privacy policy for theaha.co, operated by Dawning Inc. for a US audience.
// The analytics and cookie paragraphs follow src/data/site.ts (analytics).
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { analytics, contact } from '../data/site';

const updated = 'November 3, 2026';
const a = analytics.provider;
const address = 'Dawning Inc. (dba The Aha Company), 108 W. 13th Street, Suite 100, Wilmington, DE 19801, United States';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy policy | The Aha Company" description="How Dawning Inc. (dba The Aha Company) handles personal information on theaha.co: the contact form, Calendly scheduling, hosting and audience figures.">
  <main data-main="1">
    <section>
      <div class="lg_container">
        <div class="lg_header">
          <p class="v-eyebrow page_eyebrow">Privacy</p>
          <h1 class="intro_h1">Privacy policy</h1>
          <p class="art_lede" data-rv="privacy-lede">This site collects very little: what you send us, what you enter when you book a call, and what any website needs to be delivered. Here is what that is, what we do with it and how to reach us about it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="lg_meta">
          <div class="lg_metaitem"><span class="lg_metalabel">Last updated</span><span class="lg_metavalue" data-rv="privacy-date">{updated}</span></div>
          <div class="lg_metaitem"><span class="lg_metalabel">Operator</span><span class="lg_metavalue" data-rv="legal-entities">Dawning Inc. (dba The Aha Company)</span></div>
          <div class="lg_metaitem"><span class="lg_metalabel">Contact</span><a class="lg_metavalue" href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a></div>
        </div>
        <div class="lg_body" data-rv="privacy-body">
          <h2 class="lg_h2">Who we are</h2>
          <p>theaha.co is operated by Dawning Inc., a Delaware corporation doing business as The Aha Company (“we”, “us”), 108 W. 13th Street, Suite 100, Wilmington, DE 19801, United States. Dawning Inc. is responsible for the personal information collected through this site. This policy covers the site only: work we do for clients is governed by the agreements we sign with them.</p>

          <h2 class="lg_h2">Who this site is for</h2>
          <p>The site is intended for businesses and professionals in the United States, which is why it is in English and follows US law. It is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect information from them.</p>

          <h2 class="lg_h2">What we collect</h2>
          <ul class="lg_list" role="list">
            <li class="lg_li"><span><strong>What you send us.</strong> When you use the contact form or write to us, we receive your name, work email, company, role, the kind of organization you selected, your message and, if you came from the Networks page, the answers you gave there. {contact.formEndpoint ? 'The form sends your message to us through Formspree, which delivers it by email.' : 'The form opens your email app with your message, so it reaches us as an email you send.'}</span></li>
            <li class="lg_li"><span><strong>What you enter when you book a call.</strong> The scheduler is provided by Calendly. It collects your name, email address, the time you choose and any answers you add, and shares them with us.</span></li>
            <li class="lg_li"><span><strong>What any website needs to be delivered.</strong> Our host, Cloudflare, processes technical data such as your IP address, browser, the page requested and the time of the request, to deliver the site and protect it from abuse.</span></li>
            {a === 'umami' && <li class="lg_li" data-rv="privacy-analytics"><span><strong>Audience figures, without cookies.</strong> We count visits with Umami, which sets no cookies and does not store IP addresses. It records the page, the referring site, the browser, operating system, device type and country, and the visits that book a call, send the contact form or open an email link, and it counts unique visitors with an anonymous identifier it cannot trace back to a person. Umami stores these figures in the European Union.</span></li>}
            {a === 'plausible' && <li class="lg_li" data-rv="privacy-analytics"><span><strong>Audience figures, without cookies.</strong> We count visits with Plausible Analytics, which sets no cookies and stores no personal information. It records the page, the referring site, the browser, operating system, device type and country, and recognizes a returning visitor only within the same day, through an identifier that cannot be reversed and is deleted every 24 hours.</span></li>}
            {a === 'cloudflare' && <li class="lg_li" data-rv="privacy-analytics"><span><strong>Audience figures, without cookies.</strong> We count visits with Cloudflare Web Analytics, which sets no cookies, does not fingerprint visitors and reports only totals: page views, visits, referring sites, countries, browsers and page performance.</span></li>}
            {a === 'ga4' && <li class="lg_li" data-rv="privacy-analytics"><span><strong>Audience figures.</strong> We use Google Analytics to understand how visitors use the site. It sets cookies in your browser and collects information such as the pages you visit, how long you stay, the site that referred you, your browser and device, and your approximate location. Google processes this information for us. You can opt out with <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Google’s browser add-on</a>.</span></li>}
            {!a && <li class="lg_li" data-rv="privacy-analytics"><span><strong>Nothing else.</strong> The site runs no analytics and shows no advertising.</span></li>}
          </ul>

          <h2 class="lg_h2">How we use it</h2>
          <ul class="lg_list" role="list">
            <li class="lg_li"><span>To answer your request and hold the call you booked.</span></li>
            <li class="lg_li"><span>To prepare and follow up on a possible engagement, and to keep a record of our exchanges if we work together.</span></li>
            <li class="lg_li"><span>To run, secure and improve the site{a ? ', including counting its visitors' : ''}.</span></li>
            <li class="lg_li"><span>To comply with the law and protect our rights.</span></li>
          </ul>
          <p>We do not sell your personal information, share it for targeted advertising or use it to profile you.</p>

          <h2 class="lg_h2">Who we share it with</h2>
          <ul class="lg_list" role="list">
            <li class="lg_li" data-rv="privacy-third"><span><strong>Service providers</strong> that run parts of the site or our business for us: Cloudflare (hosting and security), Calendly (scheduling){contact.formEndpoint ? ', Formspree (contact form delivery)' : ''}{a === 'umami' ? ', Umami (audience figures)' : ''}{a === 'plausible' ? ', Plausible Analytics (audience figures)' : ''}{a === 'ga4' ? ', Google (analytics)' : ''} and our email and office software providers. They may use the information only to provide their service to us.</span></li>
            <li class="lg_li"><span><strong>Our team and affiliated companies</strong> who help answer your request, some of whom work outside the United States.</span></li>
            <li class="lg_li"><span><strong>Authorities or other parties</strong> when the law requires it, or to protect our rights and the safety of others.</span></li>
            <li class="lg_li"><span><strong>A buyer or successor</strong> if our business is merged, sold or reorganized, under this policy.</span></li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="lg_h2">Cookies and tracking</h2>
          <p data-rv="privacy-cookies">{a === 'ga4'
            ? 'The only cookies this site sets are those of Google Analytics: _ga and _ga_*, which last up to two years and tell visits apart.'
            : 'This site sets no cookies of its own.'} The Contact page loads Calendly’s scheduler as soon as it opens, so Calendly receives your IP address and browser details and may set its own cookies, under its cookie policy. Cloudflare may set a strictly necessary cookie to protect the site from automated traffic.</p>
          <p>{a === 'ga4'
            ? 'Google Analytics recognizes your browser when you come back to this site. We do not use it to follow you across other websites or for advertising, and the site does not change its behavior in response to Do Not Track signals.'
            : 'We do not track visitors over time or across other websites, so the site works the same way whether or not your browser sends a Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control signal.'} When the scheduler loads, Calendly may collect information about your use of it under its own privacy policy.</p>

          <h2 class="lg_h2">How long we keep it</h2>
          <p data-rv="privacy-retention">We keep inquiries and booking details as long as we need them to answer you and follow up, and no longer than 24 months after our last exchange, unless we start working together or the law requires us to keep them longer. Hosting logs are kept by Cloudflare under its own retention rules.</p>

          <h2 class="lg_h2">Security</h2>
          <p>We use established providers and take reasonable measures to protect the information we hold. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>

          <h2 class="lg_h2">Your choices and rights</h2>
          <p>You can ask us what personal information we hold about you, ask us to correct or delete it, or ask us to stop following up with you, by writing to <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a>. We answer within 30 days. Depending on your state, you may have additional rights under state privacy law; we honor these requests wherever you live in the United States, and we will not treat you differently for making one.</p>

          <h2 class="lg_h2">Visitors outside the United States</h2>
          <p data-rv="privacy-intl">We operate this site from the United States. If you use it or write to us from another country, your information is processed in the United States, where data protection law may differ from yours, and team members in other countries may access it under this policy. Where the EU or UK General Data Protection Regulation or a similar law applies, we use your information to answer your request and take the steps you ask for before a contract, and on our legitimate interest in running and securing this site and following up on business conversations. You can then ask for access, correction, deletion, restriction or a copy of your information, object to its use, and complain to your data protection authority.</p>

          <h2 class="lg_h2">Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>We may update this policy. The date at the top shows the latest version, and when a change is significant we say so on this page.</p>

          <h2 class="lg_h2">Contact</h2>
          <p>{address}. <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .lg_body strong { color: var(--deep-blue); font-weight: 600; }
  .lg_body a { color: var(--deep-blue); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .lg_body a:hover { color: var(--green-ink); }
</style>
